  "cited_article_id": "configure-portal-result-visibility",
  "reply": "Result visibility is controlled by release rules under **Settings > Patient Portal > Result Rules**. Click **Add Rule**, choose the lab category (e.g., Pathology or Imaging), set the **Hold Period** in hours (up to 168 h), enable **Auto‑Release**, and Save. The timer applies to all clinicians unless an order‑level override exists; critical‑flagged results skip the hold and need manual sign‑off. If a result isn’t appearing after the timer, check **Reports > Portal Log** for the auto‑release job and, if needed, use **Resend to Portal** from the patient’s chart."
}
